ded a `world_3d_changed` signal to `Viewport` because I couldn't find another clean way of updating whenever the viewport world changed. Not sure if this is best apporach, lmk. Don't like adding an API like that for no reason.~~\r\n\r\nSwitched the signal approach with a static function pointer on `Viewport` that points to `_viewport_world_3d_changed` on `Node3DEditor`.\r\n\r\nThis implementation was my idea, but AI helped a bit with some code. I have reviewed every line and tested with the test project provided here/in the issue, and my personal project that had issues with this. Seems to work fine.\r\n\r\nAlso - setting `use_world_3d` to false seems to trigger this error:\r\n`ERROR: servers\\rendering\\renderer_scene_cull.cpp:497 - Parameter \"scenario\" is null.`\r\nThis was already the case before my PR so I did not touch it.\r\n\r\nExample video:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/52ab9bf5-a7c2-4fc4-a152-c3e5fe939746\r\n\r\nExample project:\r\n[viewport_world_test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/30150780/viewport_world_test.zip)\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_i